#* {{quote-book|en|author=Arthur Lyon Raile [pseudonym; {{w|Edward Perry Warren}}]|chapter=The Uranian Idea|title=A Defence of Uranian Love|volume_plain=part the second (The Uranian Eros)|location=[London]|publisher=Privately printed|year=1930|pages=19–20|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=BJETAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA19|oclc=156094194|passage=His &#91;{{w|Plato}}'s&#93; Philosophical Eros is not the '''Uranian''' Eros which possessed the nation, and the '''Uranian''' doctrine is not primarily either philosophical or paederastic. It is a value attached to the masculine which included philosophy as masculine and paederasty when not anti-masculine, but was itself the idea and form of virtue.}}
